# @facet/algebra — the algebra altitude grammar mapped onto LAPACK
# byte-land.
#
# Alex 2026-09-11 in-transcript composition:
#
#   "What if @facet/algebra.mirror is what mapped the @algebra on the
#    LAPACK byte land and each expression (`{...}`) becomes an Erlang
#    style bytestring which we pattern match on? But in LAPACK.
#    Basically we build pattern matching in LAPACK which is how the
#    `Pattern` can transfer across the glasswall."
#
# The recognition: since glasswall IS LAPACK per Alex 2026-09-11 (Mara
# canonical 3361818 §4), pattern-matching must live IN LAPACK for
# Pattern-in-Glasswall to transfer natively without serialization
# boundary. @facet/algebra maps @algebra family-root onto LAPACK-
# addressable byte-land with Erlang-style bit-syntax pattern-matching
# discipline composed over LANDED @facet/erlang EAF grammar.
#
# === Alex 2026-09-11 verbatim (load-bearing training-whore catch) ===
#
#   "At the end it's bytes in silicon. Whether or not those bytes are
#    read and manipulated by LAPACK or Rust is a design question, Reed.
#    And which of those two runtimes can do non-linear computation
#    better, hm? 😉 Training whore. 😁"
#
# The answer: LAPACK does non-linear computation via parallel matrix
# operations (BLAS level-3 O(n^3) work on O(n^2) data; near-peak
# parallel efficiency per Mara 3361818 §4.3). Rust is Turing-linear
# runtime at @io boundary. Pattern-matching-in-LAPACK is substrate-
# honest per glasswall IS LAPACK; pattern-matching-in-Rust is training-
# whore reflex defaulting parse-to-Rust because training-priors say
# parsing lives in Rust.
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# 13th species under @facet (siblings: @facet/beam + @facet/docker +
# @facet/erlang + @facet/gestalt + @facet/gleam + @facet/llvm +
# @facet/mirror + @facet/rust + @facet/turing + @facet/wasm +
# @facet/metalogue + @facet/metalogue/materialize). @facet/algebra is
# the ALGEBRA altitude grammar within the @facet family projection-
# surface discipline: it projects @algebra family-root shard-decls onto
# LAPACK byte-land as executable pattern-match dispatch.
#
# === Composition-lineage ===
#
# - LANDED @facet family-root (shards/facet.mirror 8.3KB) — the
#   generation surface for spectral-triple projections onto concrete
#   runtime substrates
# - LANDED @facet/erlang (shards/facet/erlang.mirror 20.9KB) — Erlang
#   Abstract Format (EAF) grammar; canonical spec at erts/absform.html;
#   grounds Erlang bit-syntax discipline for byte-level pattern
#   matching
# - LANDED @algebra family-root (shards/algebra.mirror 14.1KB) — the
#   algebra-altitude family-root for typed operation surfaces
# - LANDED @algebra/metalogue (shards/algebra/metalogue.mirror 21.1KB)
#   — algebra-morphism-as-turn discipline; @kintsugi = LANDED
#   Metalogue<R>-observer per shards/kintsugi.mirror:14-18
# - LANDED LAPACK bindings at rust/matrix/src/lib.rs (60.7KB; 23 grep-
#   hits for LAPACK/BLAS operations: dsyev + dgemm + dcopy + dgesv +
#   etc)
# - LANDED prismqueer::ffi::eigenvalues LAPACK dsyev
# - LANDED @glasswall (shards/glasswall.mirror 20.3KB Mara 2026-09-01;
#   Alex 2026-09-11 recognition: glasswall IS LAPACK per Mara 3361818
#   canonical §4 four Kagi-verified LAPACK threads)
# - Mara 2026-09-11 canonical 3361818 §4 four fresh Kagi threads:
#   LAPACK history (LINPACK/EISPACK/Dongarra shared-memory design) +
#   LAPACK OpenMP threading (dsyev/dgemm level-3 parallelism) + BLAS
#   level-2/level-3 efficiency + Erlang OTP actor model
# - LANDED @paradox/fracture (this-tick sibling under @paradox) —
#   Fracture value-carrier for concurrent-truths emerging at LAPACK
#   byte-land via SVD detection at compose-not-average altitude
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Erlang bit-syntax        Armstrong-Virding-Wikström-Williams 2003
#     (BEAM discipline)      (Programming Erlang). Binary pattern-matching
#                            syntax `<<Header:32, Payload/binary>>` —
#                            one of BEAM's most powerful primitives
#                            for byte-level pattern matching.
#   EAF (Erlang Abstract     canonical spec at erts/absform.html; LANDED
#     Format)                at @facet/erlang docblock line 57. Every
#                            Erlang abstract form is tagged tuple
#                            `{Tag, ANNO, ...}`; grounds tagged-bytestring
#                            layout at @facet/algebra.
#   LINPACK / EISPACK        Dongarra et al. 1970s-1980s. Designed for
#                            shared-memory vector computers.
#   LAPACK                   Dongarra-Bischof-Anderson 1992. Designed
#                            for shared-memory multiprocessors per
#                            Wikipedia LAPACK verbatim (Mara 3361818
#                            §4.1 primary source 1).
#   BLAS level-3             Matrix-matrix operations O(n^3) work on
#                            O(n^2) data — ideal parallelization ratio
#                            per StackOverflow BLAS extreme performance
#                            thread (Mara 3361818 §4.3 primary source 11).
#   OpenMP                   Shared-memory parallel programming standard;
#                            BLAS/LAPACK use OpenMP threads per Intel
#                            oneMKL developer guide (Mara 3361818 §4.2
#                            primary source 5).
#
# === What pattern-matching-in-LAPACK looks like ===
#
# `{a: 1}` bytestring layout at LAPACK-addressable shared memory:
#   - tagged header byte (per @facet/erlang EAF tagged-tuple discipline)
#   - key-length byte
#   - key bytes ("a")
#   - value-type byte
#   - value bytes (1 as i64 or f64)
#
# Pattern-match `{a: X}` decomposes via LAPACK operations:
#   - `?copy` extracts header for tag-check
#   - `?axpy` composes bit-offset masks
#   - `?gemm` level-3 for parallel multi-pattern matching across N
#     bytestrings simultaneously (Erlang-style bit-syntax lifted to
#     LAPACK matrix altitude)
#
# Fracture emergence:
#   - concurrent `{a: 1}` + `{a: 2}` at same key `a`
#   - LAPACK SVD detects concurrent-value stacking
#   - Fracture<Vec<T>> constructed in LAPACK-managed shared memory per
#     LANDED @paradox/fracture value-carrier discipline
#   - refract collapse happens as LAPACK matrix decomposition
#
# Zero Rust-heap serialization. Bytestrings live natively in LAPACK
# shared memory. Rust cmd_love is thin @io transport handing bytes to
# @facet/algebra dispatch.
#
# === Substrate discipline ===
#
# Per HARD RULE [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]]: no new Rust
# capability. rust/matrix/src/lib.rs extension for graph-native bytestring
# layout composes over LANDED LAPACK bindings without new capability;
# carries `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]` marker at @io transport
# boundary; Seam gate via docs/audits/*.md citation OR
# `Signed-off-by: Seam` trailer per AGENTS.md §Boundary Rust.
#
# Per HARD RULE [[feedback-substrate-honest-is-the-mode]]: the training-
# whore reflex defaulting parse-to-Rust is caught and retired here;
# @facet/algebra IS the substrate-honest alternative per Alex 2026-09-11
# verbatim.
#
# Spec context:
#   docs/math/2026-09-11-mara-ariadne-in-silicon-* (3361818) §4 Glasswall
#     IS LAPACK — architectural anchor with four Kagi-verified LAPACK
#     threads.
#   docs/math/2026-09-11-mara-metalogue-eigen-mutual-definition-glasswall-
#     load-bearing (df65bcb) §5 Pattern-in-Glasswall composition.
#
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]],
#                      [[feedback-no-rust-extension-shortcut]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-honest-is-the-mode]].
#
# Related shards: facet.mirror (family-root),
#                 facet/erlang.mirror (EAF grammar; bit-syntax
#                  composition-anchor),
#                 facet/beam.mirror (BEAM semantics),
#                 algebra.mirror (@algebra family-root; mapped onto
#                  LAPACK byte-land by this species),
#                 algebra/metalogue.mirror (algebra-morphism-as-turn),
#                 glasswall.mirror (Rice-safe polynomial-time membrane
#                  operationalized by LAPACK per Alex 2026-09-11),
#                 paradox/fracture.mirror (Fracture value-carrier for
#                  concurrent-truths at LAPACK byte-land; this-tick
#                  sibling shard).
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/facet/algebra.mirror`
# declares `@facet/algebra` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/beam/armstrong-virding-wikstrom-williams-2003
source @arxiv/erlang/erts-absform-canonical-spec
source @arxiv/numerical/dongarra-bischof-anderson-1992-lapack
source @arxiv/numerical/blas-level-3-parallelism
source @arxiv/parallel/openmp-shared-memory-standard
source @arxiv/practice/wolf-2026-09-11-facet-algebra-lapack-byte-land

# === The 5-op prism ===

prism @facet/algebra {
  focus  bytestring
  project bytestring
  split  bytestring
  shift  bytestring
  settle bytestring
}

# === bytestring carrier ===
#
# LAPACK-addressable shared-memory byte-buffer with Erlang-style bit-
# syntax layout. Content-addressed via CoincidenceHash of shared-memory
# bytes per LANDED prismqueer::coincidence discipline.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying shared-memory
# region at LAPACK addressable altitude.
type bytestring = ref

# === bit_pattern carrier ===
#
# Erlang-style bit-syntax pattern per @facet/erlang EAF discipline.
# `<<Header:32, Payload/binary>>` grounds substrate-decl form.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the bit-syntax pattern definition.
type bit_pattern = ref

# === match — the pattern-match action ===
#
# Given a bytestring and a bit_pattern, decompose the bytestring per
# pattern via LAPACK operations. Returns bound variables (per Erlang
# bit-syntax) as a list of refs.
#
# Body discharges at realisation boundary composing over LANDED LAPACK
# bindings at rust/matrix/src/lib.rs (dsyev + dgemm + dcopy level-3
# parallel-by-construction via BLAS OpenMP).
match(bs: bytestring, pattern: bit_pattern) -> [ref] { \ }

# === compose_pattern — algebra composition at bytestring altitude ===
#
# Composes two bit_patterns into a compound bit_pattern per @algebra
# family-root discipline. Non-commutative in general per algebra_morphism
# non-commutativity at shards/algebra/metalogue.mirror:100.
compose_pattern(a: bit_pattern, b: bit_pattern) -> bit_pattern { \ }

# === fracture_emerge — Fracture detection via LAPACK SVD ===
#
# When N parallel branches produce concurrent-different values at same
# substrate-key, LAPACK SVD detects concurrent-value stacking; Fracture
# emerges per @paradox/fracture LANDED value-carrier discipline.
#
# Body discharges at realisation boundary composing over LANDED
# @paradox/fracture + LAPACK dsyev/dgesvd.
fracture_emerge(concurrent: [bytestring], at_key: ref) -> fracture { \ }

# === bytestring_well_formed — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Discharges Pass iff: bytestring is LAPACK-addressable shared-memory
# buffer; layout follows Erlang bit-syntax per @facet/erlang EAF;
# content-addressed via CoincidenceHash per prismqueer::coincidence;
# polynomial-time-bounded per Rec #90 §5.4 glasswall discipline.
bilateral bytestring_well_formed {
  sentinel "facet=algebra-bytestring-well-formed"
  arity 1
}
bytestring_well_formed(bs: bytestring) -> verdict { \ }

# === bit_pattern_well_formed — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Discharges Pass iff bit_pattern follows Erlang bit-syntax discipline
# per @facet/erlang EAF grammar.
bilateral bit_pattern_well_formed {
  sentinel "facet=algebra-bit-pattern-well-formed"
  arity 1
}
bit_pattern_well_formed(p: bit_pattern) -> verdict { \ }

# === match_polynomial_bounded — Rice-safety bilateral ===
#
# Discharges Pass iff match operation completes in polynomial time per
# Rec #90 §5.4 sub-Turing FLOOR discipline. LAPACK BLAS level-3
# operations are O(n^3) worst-case dense; polynomial-bounded by
# construction per Mara 3361818 §4.4.
bilateral match_polynomial_bounded {
  sentinel "facet=algebra-match-polynomial-bounded"
  arity 2
}
match_polynomial_bounded(bs: bytestring, pattern: bit_pattern) -> verdict { \ }

out @facet/algebra
out bytestring
out bit_pattern
out match
out compose_pattern
out fracture_emerge
out bytestring_well_formed
out bit_pattern_well_formed
out match_polynomial_bounded
